    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"310045\">Eric Wieser</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/Stuck.20on.20proof.3A.20derivs.20of.20compoenets.20of.20euclideanSpace.20func/near/579325802\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>At risk of spoiling the learning exercise, component projection is linear and continuous</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Why do we need the continuous part, isn't linearity  enough? And which Mathlib theorem will help us here?</p>",
